  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SVETANA: Scaling up of HIV Care and Private Sector PPTCT Services in India - India (01-Oct-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India, HIV, Solidarity and Action Against The HIV Infection in India (SAATHII)This program has the following goals: Provide comprehensive care and support to all persons living with HIV/AIDS and treatment services for all those who require it.  Reduce new infections by 50% (2007 Baseline of NACP III). The objectives of this program are: Early linkages of PLHIV including key populations to care, support and treatment services and retention in care continuum.  To improve coverage of PMTCT services through enhanced access in public and private sector and working towards ellimination of paediatric HIV and keeping mothers alive healthy.  To strengthen community systems for both HIV and TB care and reduction in stigma and discrimination</narrative>
  </description>
